## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about client-side privacy, offline UX, and cost trade-offs without server trust. The candidate must specify concrete numbers, crypto choices, and go/no-go criteria, balancing performance, storage, and regulatory costs.

## Key Concepts

- Client-side encryption and key management
- Data growth and local cache sizing
- Delta synchronization vs full sync
- Privacy/compliance implications and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example using Web Crypto API AES-GCM
async function encrypt(plaintext, cryptoKey) {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    cryptoKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
  );
  return { encrypted, iv };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model a device-resident telemetry system that serves multiple apps while enforcing data minimization and consent, balancing privacy, UX impact, and backend savings.

## Key Concepts

- Data deduplication and cross-app coordination on-device
- Consent lifecycle and policy enforcement across tenants
- On-device aggregation, sampling, and energy budgeting
- Privacy/compliance costs and drift monitoring
- Rollout strategy, break-even analysis, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
function aggregateDeltas(deltas) {
  // de-duplicate by user/app+event, then sample
  const seen = new Set();
  const out = [];
  for (const d of deltas) {
    const key = d.userId + '|' + d.appId + '|' + d.eventId;
    if (!seen.has(key)) {
      seen.add(key);
      if (Math.random() < d.sampleRate) out.push(d.aggregate);
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify cross-app dedup cost vs backend savings?
- What would a staged rollout look like to minimize risk and ensure compliance?

